(Northside Community Garden Pilot - Project Brief) Tj
T*
(Community Development Office | Pilot report | May 2025) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Northside Community Garden Pilot opened in April 2025 on a vacant) Tj
T*
(240-square-meter lot beside the neighborhood library. The project was) Tj
T*
(created to improve access to fresh produce and provide a shared place) Tj
T*
(for residents to learn practical gardening skills.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The site contains 12 raised beds, each measuring 1.2 meters by 2.4) Tj
T*
(meters. Eight beds are used for vegetables, two for herbs, and two for) Tj
T*
(seasonal flowers that attract pollinators. Wide paths allow wheelchair) Tj
T*
(access to the central beds and tool shed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The first-season plan prioritizes tomatoes, leafy greens, beans, and) Tj
T*
(culinary herbs. Volunteers label each bed and record planting dates in) Tj
T*
(a shared garden log. Produce is distributed without charge to local) Tj
T*
(households participating in the weekly harvest table.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
