stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
50 760 Td
16 TL
(Operations and Community Participation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The pilot serves 48 Northside households. A roster of 28 volunteers) Tj
T*
(supports planting, watering, repairs, and the weekly harvest table.) Tj
T*
(Volunteer work parties are held on Saturday mornings from April through) Tj
T*
(October. The garden coordinator is responsible for safety checks and) Tj
T*
(the monthly inventory of tools and supplies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The garden uses approximately 600 liters of water each week during the) Tj
T*
(growing season. Two rainwater barrels supply part of this demand, and) Tj
T*
(drip irrigation delivers water directly to plant roots. Water use is) Tj
T*
(recorded every Friday to help the volunteers identify leaks or waste.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A three-bin compost system processes about 180 kilograms of plant) Tj
T*
(trimmings and food scraps per month. Meat, dairy, and cooking oils are) Tj
T*
(not accepted. Finished compost is added to the raised beds twice a) Tj
T*
(year, in spring and autumn.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
