<< /Length 1097 >>
stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
50 760 Td
16 TL
(First-Season Results and Learning) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The first growing season produced 220 kilograms of tomatoes and 140) Tj
T*
(kilograms of leafy greens. Herbs and beans were also harvested, but) Tj
T*
(their weights were not recorded. The harvest table distributed produce) Tj
T*
(to participating households every Wednesday from June through October.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Sixteen free workshops were delivered during the first season. Topics) Tj
T*
(included seed starting, water-wise gardening, composting, and safe food) Tj
T*
(handling. The end-of-season survey reported that 85 percent of) Tj
T*
(responding households were satisfied with the garden program.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The pilot received a one-time city grant of 4,800 dollars. The largest) Tj
T*
(expenses were soil and lumber for the raised beds. The grant report) Tj
T*
(does not provide an itemized amount for each expense category.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Next season, the coordinator plans to measure herb and bean harvests,) Tj
T*
(review water records, and invite more residents to the workshops.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
